<title>Philippines: Philippine forex market closed.</title>
<headline>Philippine forex market closed.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Nov 25 -------------------------</p>
<p>* Thin trading in grey market</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine Dealing System (PDS)</p>
<p>remained closed on Monday due to the summit meeting of the Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC).</p>
<p>The PDS is the computerised peso-dollar trading system among banks.</p>
<p>Traders, however, said banks continued to deal among themselves in the grey market where volume remained thin.  </p>
<p>There was a done rate of 26.35 pesos to the dollar in the grey market, which is off the last done deal of 26.278 pesos in Thursday's session before the PDS closed, a dealer said.</p>
<p>- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841 8937</p>
